WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.958 --> 00:00:09.000
…we don't know how -
that doesn't matter.

00:00:09.083 --> 00:00:11.000
What we'd like to know is...

00:00:13.333 --> 00:00:15.917
What would a world
without humans be like?

00:00:23.292 --> 00:00:28.125
Within days, the electricity grid
fails as fuel supplies run out

00:00:28.208 --> 00:00:32.292
and there's nobody to override the
powerstation's failsafe mechanisms.

00:00:33.083 --> 00:00:37.625
Within a week the subways we've
built under the water table flood.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.333
The 47 million litres of water

00:00:40.417 --> 00:00:43.500
that was pumped out of
the London Underground every day

00:00:43.583 --> 00:00:45.167
inundates tunnels.

00:00:46.042 --> 00:00:48.167
Without heating or air conditioning

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:51.875
mould flourishes on moist surfaces
in homes and offices

00:00:51.958 --> 00:00:54.250
and ice bursts pipes.

00:00:54.833 --> 00:00:58.667
Within weeks, plants begin
to take over buildings

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:01.833
as the strongest species
compete for space.

00:01:02.167 --> 00:01:04.250
No-one's there to cut them back.

00:01:05.083 --> 00:01:06.792
Fast forward in time.

00:01:07.292 --> 00:01:11.042
The lines between city
and countryside are blurred.

00:01:11.708 --> 00:01:16.292
Windows fall out of rotten frames
and wildlife recolonises towns.

00:01:17.083 --> 00:01:21.042
Farmland is blanketed
by scrub and then trees,

00:01:21.833 --> 00:01:26.083
and scattered on the surface are
the things that will never degrade.

00:01:26.917 --> 00:01:31.292
Metals corrode. Plastics start
to break down and disperse.

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:35.167
But stainless steel pans,
stranded granite work tops

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:37.875
and billions of car tyres remain.

00:01:38.875 --> 00:01:42.125
Nuclear facilities fail
as their fabric degrades.

00:01:42.583 --> 00:01:46.083
Some explode,
irradiating the local ecosystem

00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:48.667
and causing many animals to die.

00:01:49.417 --> 00:01:52.083
The radiation leads
to mutations in others

00:01:52.167 --> 00:01:54.750
creating new evolutionary lines.

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:57.583
Meanwhile, the tiniest of plants

00:01:57.667 --> 00:02:00.833
are stubbornly breaking up
even the motorways.

00:02:01.625 --> 00:02:03.792
Mosquitos are having a great time.

00:02:03.875 --> 00:02:05.625
They've lost their enemy in us

00:02:05.708 --> 00:02:07.958
but they've moved on
to other animals.

00:02:08.042 --> 00:02:12.792
And they're busy pollinating plants
as they love nectar as well as blood.

00:02:13.375 --> 00:02:16.875
Endangered animals have a chance
and space to multiply again.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:20.125
Lions and elephants
could even reach Europe,

00:02:20.208 --> 00:02:23.667
the strongest swimming
across the Suez Canal.

00:02:24.125 --> 00:02:28.625
Massive whirlpool islands of plastic
carry on spinning in our oceans.

00:02:29.375 --> 00:02:32.208
Each piece of plastic is ground down

00:02:32.292 --> 00:02:35.375
until microscopic grains
of it are everywhere.

00:02:36.042 --> 00:02:38.958
Bacteria may evolve
to digest plastic,

00:02:39.458 --> 00:02:42.042
but this will take millions of years.

00:02:42.833 --> 00:02:44.792
Could the Earth ever recover?

00:02:45.208 --> 00:02:48.083
Atmospheric carbon dioxide
is absorbed

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:50.458
by the vegetation that
carpets the land.

00:02:50.958 --> 00:02:54.500
Global temperatures
and sea levels begin to fall.

00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:58.750
As chemical pollutants break down
and sink into the earth,

00:02:58.833 --> 00:03:00.542
rivers become cleaner.

00:03:00.625 --> 00:03:02.792
Animals and plants flourish.

00:03:03.125 --> 00:03:04.833
Is this a new Eden?

00:03:04.917 --> 00:03:06.250
Perhaps.

00:03:06.333 --> 00:03:08.333
The Earth is a breathing organism

00:03:08.417 --> 00:03:11.333
that has lived with us
for a fraction of its life.

00:03:12.042 --> 00:03:16.958
Our human ingenuity has led to
extraordinary changes to the world.

00:03:17.542 --> 00:03:21.667
The planet would survive,
indeed thrive, without us.

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:24.417
But it would never be able
to forget us.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.920
We'd have left our mark.

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:30.320
Thanks for watching.

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:34.440
Don't forget to subscribe and click the bell to receive notifications for new videos.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:35.620
See you again soon!

